[{:db/id "q-334072/selection/1df72a42ae6ce0eeb848cc612ec18ad01b5266e34a7ae355a0e347c54077d99d" :answer/id #uuid "1e33e08a-3d11-5267-91f1-7d3ddd583be3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{3}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072/selection/0a4731710025ba10eeed887b2293e48fb5c0b84aee3c9c5079fda0c4fef0f9fc" :answer/id #uuid "6f95f36e-2cf1-571c-9514-fa59a20b08ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072/selection/6921b2661240705c5c69abae30eb94c0a625c81320cdca52fca8b0efeea58785" :answer/id #uuid "4e5f3592-8fd4-5bc5-950c-dfa6fd085f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-6\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072/selection/05320af95aebb9d3f457411af62e3da824a12d4d4a6641f1d48b4f1504e79ef2" :answer/id #uuid "383a9302-0349-5654-8bdc-e0e464d1c568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072/selection/7d598dfecc69dce021edd49b85c54eb925e4a47c4fdb6109092043e30d794402" :answer/id #uuid "9ca2e251-88f2-5c8b-9d5e-f815c2edd54f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "067f8362-bbc5-529d-af2a-79c89a8a70b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334072/selection/7d598dfecc69dce021edd49b85c54eb925e4a47c4fdb6109092043e30d794402" :answer-field/choices ["q-334072/selection/1df72a42ae6ce0eeb848cc612ec18ad01b5266e34a7ae355a0e347c54077d99d" "q-334072/selection/0a4731710025ba10eeed887b2293e48fb5c0b84aee3c9c5079fda0c4fef0f9fc" "q-334072/selection/6921b2661240705c5c69abae30eb94c0a625c81320cdca52fca8b0efeea58785" "q-334072/selection/05320af95aebb9d3f457411af62e3da824a12d4d4a6641f1d48b4f1504e79ef2" "q-334072/selection/7d598dfecc69dce021edd49b85c54eb925e4a47c4fdb6109092043e30d794402"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334072" :question/id #uuid "872582af-4f14-53f7-9ee8-179fc32d0c45" :question/math-academy-id "q-334072" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+6\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}+3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{{{y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\,{y}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-y-3\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334072/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection/4e3a08993c651ef656d2b7ed775d9f747ff607a109625bc1c046324ae62a8530" :answer/id #uuid "5f1e0ced-9569-5168-b33f-f29d7cf19154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection/a93ba937a59d3514c1a34cf0b794b2836d29b8ac4af78ac2f97615ef69cd59d2" :answer/id #uuid "4a90a6e4-0ed4-5807-85a2-cad515a8a9ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection/3b808c285da235dcaf0a5d33ccc5d5a52d9f4da2498e15c00ac81d5dd3252848" :answer/id #uuid "4c9d1d96-6f3c-5fd9-b43c-a44e3683e9d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection/f3baca0fe226b6ec07d739f6125c9f9124d5ef38e19e27f3f173173070dde8a0" :answer/id #uuid "285e2475-4b47-5219-8a94-024f5eccbe15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection/a763ceec3273e947ce5bbcdcc00e7a1554e5d8169740cda54107453607d968b5" :answer/id #uuid "338b4665-3a5e-5508-b6f0-a7bfe1198443" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6533f3-0198-5a41-a1ef-b0cf440a7dca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334077/selection/a93ba937a59d3514c1a34cf0b794b2836d29b8ac4af78ac2f97615ef69cd59d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-334077/selection/4e3a08993c651ef656d2b7ed775d9f747ff607a109625bc1c046324ae62a8530" "q-334077/selection/a93ba937a59d3514c1a34cf0b794b2836d29b8ac4af78ac2f97615ef69cd59d2" "q-334077/selection/3b808c285da235dcaf0a5d33ccc5d5a52d9f4da2498e15c00ac81d5dd3252848" "q-334077/selection/f3baca0fe226b6ec07d739f6125c9f9124d5ef38e19e27f3f173173070dde8a0" "q-334077/selection/a763ceec3273e947ce5bbcdcc00e7a1554e5d8169740cda54107453607d968b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334077" :question/id #uuid "c3e7b77a-8724-5c98-839a-9b13b32a04b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-334077" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}\\sqrt{y},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334077/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection/540204898b6742453eaa9c37689235219126f207f9b84c0257a68260f313a73a" :answer/id #uuid "f8684226-533e-5a22-84cb-5d072933d3c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection/9289d9352ba1d0beaf986a0af87f19a601430736019dbb171e8871c8832780e4" :answer/id #uuid "f9ecbfc0-1949-5540-a1e8-8ed9fe3534b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection/a4e5089c3e7d087e15a12cd1b27ece63ac120a964379a1e70d9e345451151017" :answer/id #uuid "47d79dfc-70ce-57b0-86d1-484bd4cada5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection/3466b6de826793a65b652b469be79239debeb27195c2b88f61c6278aa6a749d3" :answer/id #uuid "56d5e153-950c-5595-ae6c-15d9ec062d12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection/ebf8c6ca6c750d215a8290114cb484d674bb09edc649e7d4f051e952d179138e" :answer/id #uuid "2ae12989-38db-5624-b104-090ef10a0318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22c64eb7-5d70-57e1-b5c4-62cddb992905" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334080/selection/ebf8c6ca6c750d215a8290114cb484d674bb09edc649e7d4f051e952d179138e" :answer-field/choices ["q-334080/selection/540204898b6742453eaa9c37689235219126f207f9b84c0257a68260f313a73a" "q-334080/selection/9289d9352ba1d0beaf986a0af87f19a601430736019dbb171e8871c8832780e4" "q-334080/selection/a4e5089c3e7d087e15a12cd1b27ece63ac120a964379a1e70d9e345451151017" "q-334080/selection/3466b6de826793a65b652b469be79239debeb27195c2b88f61c6278aa6a749d3" "q-334080/selection/ebf8c6ca6c750d215a8290114cb484d674bb09edc649e7d4f051e952d179138e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334080" :question/id #uuid "27c9463d-3427-5712-975e-bf5711e6e029" :question/math-academy-id "q-334080" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-y,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example  $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}^{2}-y)+({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-y+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}).\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-1+{2}^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(0+4-{y}_{\\text{new}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334449/field-1/ccbaf511fce424dba66b8576ce46b4bdb2c44aeadf146e7120e6330c699a2ea1" :answer/id #uuid "af5a605f-b602-5a1d-a22d-2370f6a44316" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334449/field-1/7c2fec16fd7ae02af1a8818a9096a676afc42249e7e68d108c3f64859048a45f" :answer/id #uuid "bc56e5e1-6859-5093-8182-07bc4f9de9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228128 :answer-field/correct "q-334449/field-1/ccbaf511fce424dba66b8576ce46b4bdb2c44aeadf146e7120e6330c699a2ea1" :answer-field/choices ["q-334449/field-1/ccbaf511fce424dba66b8576ce46b4bdb2c44aeadf146e7120e6330c699a2ea1" "q-334449/field-1/7c2fec16fd7ae02af1a8818a9096a676afc42249e7e68d108c3f64859048a45f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334449"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=-1.4\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})+({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+y-{y}_{\\text{new}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5{x}^{2}+0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+y-{y}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\n Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5(1)^{2}+0.5(-1.4)^{3}+0.5(2)^{2}-1.4-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+0.5-1.372+2-1.4-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.272.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=-1.4$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}-({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-0.272}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1)=-1.4,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =-1.4 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈-1.274\\,227 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈-1.251\\,778 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈-1.251\\,069\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-1.25,$ rounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334472/field-1/952fdacdf904e9f342066d0e457b21a19888fb9527d5c8df8cda695730ec4bc9" :answer/id #uuid "580d28f6-59b0-5f7b-b3c0-ef57313a6b98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.46" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334472/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d064b82-c9d7-537f-9e41-44c0a81f6906" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334472/field-1/952fdacdf904e9f342066d0e457b21a19888fb9527d5c8df8cda695730ec4bc9" :answer-field/choices ["q-334472/field-1/952fdacdf904e9f342066d0e457b21a19888fb9527d5c8df8cda695730ec4bc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334472" :question/id #uuid "ba5bf65e-2048-5ca1-a76d-755a9f7b9749" :question/math-academy-id "q-334472" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\,Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.5{x}^{2}-0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+0.5{x}^{2}-0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\n$$\n\nMoving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-0.5{x}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-0.5{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\n Then the function $g$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5(1)^{3}-1-0.5\\cdot {2}^{2}-0.5\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-3}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈1.600\\,00 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.466\\,116 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.456\\,216\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈1.46,$ rounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334472/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e885f33-5bef-5c95-8afa-495b6512e398"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
